// `f` captures itself before its value exists, so its register r0 in `outer`
// gets a fresh cell (`NewCell`) before the `Closure` is made, and `SetCell`
// writes the closure into that cell. (At the top level `f` would be a global,
// which needs no cell.) What it returns contains itself, which only an `Any`
// holds.
// compile: analysed
fn outer() { fn f() -> Any { f } }
